# Python Virtual Environment

All Python development in this workspace uses the local Python 3.13 virtual environment.

## Paths

| Item | Path |
|---|---|
| Venv root | `.venv/` |
| Python executable | `.venv\Scripts\python.exe` |
| Pip executable | `.venv\Scripts\pip.exe` |
| Site-packages | `.venv\Lib\site-packages\` |
| Python version | 3.13 (system install at `C:\Users\kanis\AppData\Local\Python\pythoncore-3.13-64\python.exe`) |

## Command Rules

### Always use the venv Python — never the system Python

```powershell
# ❌ BAD — uses system Python
python script.py
pip install requests

# ❌ BAD — uses py launcher directly (system Python)
py -3.13 script.py

# ✅ GOOD — uses venv Python
.venv\Scripts\python.exe script.py
.venv\Scripts\pip.exe install requests
```

### Shortcut: activate venv for the session

```powershell
# Activate once, then use python/pip directly
.venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
python script.py
pip install requests
```

### Package management

```powershell
# Install packages
.venv\Scripts\pip.exe install <package>

# Install from requirements
.venv\Scripts\pip.exe install -r requirements.txt

# Freeze dependencies
.venv\Scripts\pip.exe freeze > requirements.txt

# List installed packages
.venv\Scripts\pip.exe list
```

### Running tools (pytest, ruff, mypy, etc.)

```powershell
# After installing tools
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m ruff check .
.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m mypy --strict .
```

## Creating the Venv (reference only — already created)

```powershell
# If the venv needs to be recreated:
py -3.13 -m venv .venv
.venv\Scripts\pip.exe install --upgrade pip
```

## Anti-Patterns

| Anti-Pattern | Correct Behavior |
|---|---|
| `python script.py` (system Python) | `.venv\Scripts\python.exe script.py` |
| `pip install pkg` (system pip) | `.venv\Scripts\pip.exe install pkg` |
| `py -3.13 script.py` (bypasses venv) | `.venv\Scripts\python.exe script.py` |
| `python -m venv .venv` (may pick wrong Python) | `py -3.13 -m venv .venv` (creation only) |
| Installing packages globally | Always install into `.venv` |
